Usage:

```tsx
<CheckoutScreen
  items={cartItems}
  deliveryFee={4.99}
  onBack={() => navigate("/cart")}
  onPay={(address) => submitOrder(address)}
/>
```

Notes:
- CSS variables (`--tg-theme-*`) pick up Telegram's native theme automatically when `Telegram.WebApp` injects them on `document.documentElement`; fallbacks keep it usable outside Telegram.
- Validation runs on blur and on submit; `onPay` only fires once the form is valid.
- The "Back to cart" button and the back-arrow icon both call `onBack`, so there are two ways back as is typical in Mini Apps (header chevron + footer button).
